  "knownIssues": [
    {
      "severity": "Bug",
      "area": "Publish/Unpublish (Nine-Grid Completed list)",
      "summary": "Clicking Publish/Unpublish as a caller who is NOT the cycle's direct MyManager throws an unhandled server exception (HTTP 500 from Service/MgScanService.asmx/SetManagementScanPublishState) instead of a graceful authorization error. STILL PRESENT in this release - reproduced a FOURTH time (2026-08-10 x2, 2026-08-12, 2026-08-13), identical response body each time. Still not filed as an ADO bug.",
      "reproduction": "Log in as the org-level account one level above the evaluator (not the candidate's direct MyManager), open Nine-Grid, Generate, select the candidate's cell, click Publish/Unpublish on their row.",
      "evidence": "Response body: {\"Message\":\"There was an error processing the request.\",\"StackTrace\":\"\",\"ExceptionType\":\"\"}"
    },
    {
      "severity": "Confirmed release",
      "area": "Manager assessment - open questions removed (PR 5665 / ADR-015)",
      "summary": "Fingerprint-checked directly: the Manager/evaluator's assessment play-through now renders 28 questions (not 31) - the 3 open-context questions are gone from that side, while the assessed person (Candidate) still gets all 31. Confirms this run is testing a genuinely new release, not a repeat of the 2026-08-10/2026-08-12 build.",
      "reproduction": "Complete the evaluator side of a fresh assessment cycle and count rendered .mgscan-question elements."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Fixed - verified working",
      "area": "PDF/HTML report generation - now unified across ALL surfaces",
      "summary": "A 'Unify Manager and Employee report generation' change in this release moved the Personal Dashboard's Report(HTML)/(PDF) buttons onto the same language-popup flow already used by the Nine-Grid toolbar and row-level reports. All five report-generation paths tested this run produced a real result: Personal Dashboard PDF (real download), Personal Dashboard HTML (opens a tab, no download - expected for HTML), Nine-Grid toolbar PDF (real download), row-level PDF (real download), row-level HTML (opens a tab). The first attempt at testing the Personal Dashboard flow hung for 30s - the old test code assumed an immediate download and left the HTML popup open, blocking the PDF button underneath; fixed to detect and handle the popup on every report surface consistently.",
      "reproduction": "Any Report (HTML) or Report (PDF) button, Personal Dashboard or Nine-Grid, toolbar or row-level."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Needs follow-up",
      "area": "Assessment validation banner - not observed within 10s on submit-without-answering",
      "summary": "Submitting with zero questions answered still correctly highlights every required question (.is-unanswered, 30 of 31 - the 1 optional trailing question is correctly excluded) via the client-side showValidation(true) flag, which fires synchronously and is unaffected by the server round-trip. But the textual validation banner (bound to the errorMessage observable, set from the CompleteManagementScan server response) did not appear within a 10-second wait this run - a longer wait than the 2026-08-10/2026-08-12 runs needed (both found it within ~1.5s). Not confirmed as a regression - could be a slower server round-trip in this release, or a genuine change to when/whether errorMessage gets populated - worth a manual check before concluding either way.",
      "reproduction": "Log in as an account with no manager relationship, start the assessment, submit without answering anything."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Known limitation (test script, not product)",
      "area": "Chosen multi-select filter reset",
      "summary": "Clicking a staged filter chip's .search-choice-close icon does not remove it in this build/config of the Chosen widget - confirmed safely bounded (the test's safety cap stops after 1 attempt with a clear note) rather than hanging indefinitely, which is what happened before this was found and fixed. Selecting a filter value works correctly and reliably; only the programmatic clear-via-click-icon path doesn't behave as expected. Needs live browser inspection to find the right interaction (not a blocker for this report).",
      "reproduction": "Select a real value in the Department/Function/Supervisor filter, then attempt to click its chip's close icon."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Good (by design)",
      "area": "Kalibirity manual override (position swatches)",
      "summary": "The unauthorized org-rollup account's manual-override swatches remain correctly non-actionable (30s timeout, no data mutation possible) - confirmed again this run, consistent with ADR-001 authorization intent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Process fix (already applied, carried forward)",
      "area": "create-mgscan-test-accounts.mjs merge-by-role fix",
      "summary": "Fixed 2026-08-12: creating a second batch of accounts under the same runStamp used to silently overwrite results/account-setup-<runStamp>.json instead of merging. Confirmed working correctly this run (4 accounts accumulated in one file across 2 separate creation calls, no data loss) - but surfaced a follow-on bug: test-assessment-validation.mjs picked account index [0] to find the validation-only account, which was only ever safe when that account was alone in its file. Fixed 2026-08-13 to look up by role instead."
    }
  ],
  "terminologyNote": "Reported roles are the feature's own two-role model ONLY - \"Manager\" (the person being assessed) and \"Director\" (their evaluator). A third org-hierarchy account one level above the evaluator exists only to demonstrate the Publish/Unpublish 500 bug in Known Issues and is not a timed role in this report."
}